'''''Metrosideros stipularis''''' is a species of the [[Myrtaceae|myrtle family]] commonly known as '''tepú''', '''trepú''', or '''tepual'''. It is an evergreen tree or shrub that attains heights of about four to five metres.{{sfn|Donoso|2007|p=591}} The plant is native to southern [[South America]] in the southern portions of [[Chile]] and [[Argentina]] and is a typical resident of very wet areas, especially in [[swamp]]s{{sfn|Bannister|2018|p=11}} and [[peat bog]]s and with [[gleyic]] [[soil horizon]]s.{{sfn|Donoso|2007|p=592}}{{sfn|Bannister|2018|p=34}} Tepú has white flowers that emerge during the austral summer from December through April, but more commonly from Frebruary to March.{{sfn|Bannister|2018|p=25}} The species is [[Shade tolerance|shade tolerant]] and grows merkedly slowly, less than 1 mm per year.{{sfn|Donoso|2007|p=592}} Mature tepú forest or '''tepuales''' have high [[basal area]]s when compared with other types of humid forests.{{sfn|Bannister|2018|p=33}} Tepú trees tend to grow horizontally and Tepú forest tend have high [[biomass]] contents.{{sfn|Bannister|2018|p=11}} 

In some localities it grows together with ''[[Fitzroya cupressoides]]'' or with ''[[Pilgerodendron uviferum]]''.{{sfn|Bannister|2018|p=11}} The tepu is most abundant in the Chilean provinces of [[Chiloé Province|Chiloé]], [[Llanquihue Province|Llanquihue]] and [[Palena Province|Palena]].{{sfn|Bannister|2018|p=11}}

The tree's wood is hard and used within its range as a firewood due to it high energy content.{{sfn|Donoso|2007|p=592}}<ref>{{Cite book |last=Hoffmann |first=A. |title=Flora silvestre de Chile zona araucana |date=1982 |publisher=Ediciones Fundación Claudio Gay |edition=4th |location=Santiago, Chile |page=258 |language=es}}</ref> It is commonly recommended to use its firewood mixed with wood from other species given its excessive heat content that is said to be able to break [[kitchen stove]]s.{{sfn|Donoso|2007|p=592}}

This species has often been placed in its own genus ''Tepualia'', but recent works include it in ''[[Metrosideros]]''.<ref name="Pillon 2015" /><ref>{{cite web|url=http://apps.kew.org/wcsp/|title=WCSP |work= World Checklist of Selected Plant Families}}</ref>

